# Security Review: `app.js`

## Overview

The file is a minimal Express app with three endpoints: `/health`, `/users`, and a listener on port 3000. While small, it has several concrete weaknesses and is missing many baseline protections that any Express service should have. There are no SQL queries, user input handlers, or auth flows present, so some classic categories (SQLi, broken auth) don't directly apply *yet* — but the app is wide open in other ways.

