---

### 7. No global error handler — leaks stack traces (OWASP A05 / A09) — **Medium**

Without an error-handling middleware, Express's default handler will return stack traces in development mode and inconsistent responses in production. Add one:

```js
// Must be the LAST middleware
app.use((err, req, res, _next) => {
  req.log?.error({ err }, 'unhandled error'); // structured log, no PII
  res.status(err.status || 500).json({ error: 'Internal Server Error' });
});
```

Also handle process-level failures so a crash doesn't leave the server in a bad state:

```js
process.on('unhandledRejection', (err) => { console.error(err); process.exit(1); });
process.on('uncaughtException',  (err) => { console.error(err); process.exit(1); });
```

