## Summary

`app.js` is a small Express application with three endpoints (`/health`, `/users`, and an implicit listener on port 3000). It is short, but it has several **real security concerns** and is missing many baseline protections you'd want before exposing it to a network. Below I walk through findings mapped to the OWASP Top 10, then give concrete code recommendations.

