const HOST = process.env.HOST || '127.0.0.1';
app.listen(PORT, HOST, () => console.log(`Server running on ${HOST}:${PORT}`));
```

Also: when behind a proxy, set `app.set('trust proxy', 1);` so rate-limiting and `req.ip` work correctly.

---

### 11. No HTTPS / TLS Enforcement (OWASP A02)

**Issue:** App listens on plain HTTP. In production, TLS should be terminated at a proxy (nginx, ALB) and HTTP should redirect or be refused. Combined with HSTS via helmet.

